5. Third-Party Library Licenses

MoldEZ incorporates several open-source libraries, each used solely for
internal academic research and compatible with this Agreement's non-commercial
terms. All rights in these libraries remain with their respective owners.

    tkinter (PSF License), Pillow/PIL (MIT-CMU), NumPy (BSD), SciPy (BSD),
    Matplotlib (BSD-compatible), OpenCV/cv2 (Apache 2.0, v4.5.0+), ReportLab
    (BSD), and tkinterdnd2 (Public Domain) are used for GUI, image processing,
    computation, visualization, and report generation. Roboflow (Apache 2.0
    client SDK) is used for AI-assisted dish detection and culture segmentation.
    pillow-heif (BSD-3-Clause) is used for HEIC/HEIF image support; its bundled
    libheif library carries GPL-2.0+ terms, which are compatible with the
    current internal academic deployment but must be reviewed if distribution
    is ever expanded.

    No third-party library listed above grants any rights to MoldEZ's own
    source code, algorithms, trained models, or compiled outputs beyond the
    terms set forth in this Agreement.


